# Frontend build-time configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables reach the browser bundle. Nothing here is a
# secret — the API's address is visible in the network tab on the first request.

# Origin of the SANKHYA API.
#
# Leave this EMPTY for local development: the app then calls /api/* and Vite's
# proxy forwards it to localhost:8000, so the browser stays on one origin and
# there is no CORS preflight on every request.
#
# In production, prefer a host-level rewrite from /api/* to the API and leave
# this empty too — same-origin costs nothing and avoids CORS entirely. Set it
# only when the frontend host cannot rewrite, in which case the API's
# CORS_ORIGINS must list this site's origin.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
